# 10. IMPORTANT SECURITY HEADERS

Common security-related HTTP headers include:

| Header | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Content-Security-Policy | Helps control allowed content sources |
| Strict-Transport-Security | Helps enforce HTTPS |
| X-Content-Type-Options | Helps prevent MIME-type sniffing |
| Referrer-Policy | Controls referrer information |
| Permissions-Policy | Controls certain browser features |

### Important

Security headers improve security but **do not automatically make an application secure**.

