# 47. COMMON WEB SECURITY MISTAKES

### Mistake 1

Trusting client-side validation.

**Fix:** Validate on the server.

### Mistake 2

Hiding an admin button and assuming authorization is secure.

**Fix:** Enforce authorization server-side.

### Mistake 3

Storing passwords in plaintext.

**Fix:** Use an appropriate password-hashing scheme.

### Mistake 4

Displaying stack traces to users.

**Fix:** Use safe user-facing errors and secure server-side logging.

### Mistake 5

Assuming HTTPS fixes all vulnerabilities.

**Fix:** HTTPS protects transport; application vulnerabilities can still exist.

### Mistake 6

Trusting third-party dependencies blindly.

**Fix:** Monitor and assess dependencies.

### Mistake 7

Logging passwords or tokens.

**Fix:** Protect sensitive secrets from logs.

